Enable the DPP gemm kernel for gfx101x.

Remnant of composable-kernel-7.1.0-expand-isa.patch (Gentoo bug 947583,
ROCm/composable_kernel#775). ROCm 10.0 upstreamed almost all of that patch:
ck.hpp's CK_BUFFER_RESOURCE_3RD_DWORD and FMA ladders, ck_tile/core/config.hpp's
__gfx101__ definition (upstream's is broader, also covering gfx1013 and
gfx10_1_generic) and its CK_TILE_BUFFER_RESOURCE_3RD_DWORD ladder, plus the six
device_*_dl.hpp headers -- 20 of the original 21 hunks are now redundant.

Only this one is still missing: kernel_gemm_dpp() guards on
__gfx103__/__gfx11__/__gfx12__ (upstream added gfx12 but not gfx101), so a
gfx1010/1011/1012 build still compiles an empty kernel body.
verified 2026-08-29 against the therock-10.0 composablekernel asset.
